 "documents": {
  "attachments": [
   {
    "name": "ambulance_agreement.txt",
    "text": "Lifeline Event Medics\nBookings Office\n\n18 July 2027\n\nDear Tomas Reyes,\n\nThank you for your booking and payment. This letter is your agreement with us for ambulance cover at the Firefighters' Fund Open Race Half Marathon on 24 October 2027. One ambulance and two paramedics will be on site at the pavilion, in place by 08:30, and will stay until the race has finished. Booking reference AG-75568.\n\nOur crew leader will find your race director when they arrive.\n\nKind regards,\nFatima Haddad\nBookings Manager\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "crowd_plan.txt",
    "text": "Firefighters' Fund Open Race Half Marathon - crowd notes\nSunday 24 October 2027 / contact Tomas Reyes 555-0170\ntotal 650 incl 650 runners. We do not expect spectators in any number beyond the runners' own companions.\n\nVIEWING\n3 barriered areas: finish the boathouse, turn at Pier Promenade, start the pavilion. approx 850 total @ 2 per sqm. over expected numbers\n\nSTART\n3 waves, 4 min gaps, seeded by expected time. pens close 5 min before each wave\n\nSTEWARDS\n13 stewards (approx 1:50), 2 supervisors, rota by position, briefing 1hr before\n\nEXIT\nrunners one-way funnel to recovery, out north gate. spectators 2 marked exits, steward on each. clear in 25 mins\n\nCONTROL\nTomas Reyes at control w/ radio to all supervisors. can hold wave, stop race, use PA. sups call in if area getting full\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "Harbourline Insurance Company\nCertificate of Insurance\n\nWe certify that a policy of event public liability insurance has been issued as follows.\n\nPolicy: PL-971352\nInsured: Halden Firefighters' Benevolent Fund\nEvent covered: Firefighters' Fund Open Race Half Marathon\nLocation of event: South Pier\nCover starts: 1 January 2027\nCover ends: 31 December 2027\nLimit of indemnity: $2,000,000 any one event\n\nSigned on behalf of the insurer, 18 July 2027\nCertificate reference RQ-98853\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "EVENT MEDICAL PLAN\nFirefighters' Fund Open Race Half Marathon, Sunday 24 October 2027\nApplicant: Halden Firefighters' Benevolent Fund\nIssue: 3.2\n\n1. Event summary\nA half marathon race with 650 runners, starting at 09:30 in the South Pier area of Port Halden. An ambulance from Lifeline Event Medics is on site for the race; the paperwork is attached.\n\n2. First aid cover\n3 first aid posts will operate, at the start, at the finish and at the course midpoint, staffed by 10 qualified first aiders. Posts are placed so that no part of the course is more than 1.5 km from one. Two cycle responders move along the course with defibrillators.\n\n3. Weather and hydration\nWater is available every 2.5 km. The race director checks the forecast 48 hours and 2 hours before the start. Above 28 degrees C the start is brought forward or the course shortened, and above 32 degrees C the race is cancelled. In cold or wet conditions, foil blankets and a warm shelter are at the finish.\n\n4. Transfer to hospital\nThe receiving hospital is Harbourside Medical Centre, 5 km from the finish. The transfer route and the pick-up point at the pavilion have been walked with the first aid team. The hospital's emergency department has been told the date and the expected numbers.\n\n5. Communications\nEvery first aid post and cycle responder carries a radio on the medical channel, with phones as backup. All calls for an ambulance go through the medical lead, who gives the crew the access point and the nearest barrier to open.\n\n6. Clinical lead\nThe medical lead is Patrick Doyle, a registered paramedic, who is on site from an hour before the start until the last runner is cleared. The lead can have any runner withdrawn on medical grounds.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "RACE PLAN\nFirefighters' Fund Open Race Half Marathon | Sunday 24 October 2027\nOrganiser: Halden Firefighters' Benevolent Fund\nRace director: Tomas Reyes\nReference: AG-77119\n\nOverview\nThe Firefighters' Fund Open Race Half Marathon is a half marathon race of 21 km for 650 entrants, based in the South Pier area of Port Halden. The start is at 09:30 and the course closes at 13:00.\n\nCourse\nThe course stays entirely on the Reservoir Walk and the Pier Promenade, away from the highway, and no road is closed for the race. The finish is at the boathouse.\n\nCourse dimensions\nUsable width on the Reservoir Walk is 8 m and on the Pier Promenade 12 m, with lawn or open paving beside the course for almost the whole distance. The finish area measures roughly 120 m by 60 m.\n\nSupport\nEntrants collect numbers from the pavilion from one hour before the start. Timing is by chip, with mats at the start and finish. Results are posted on the Firefighters' Fund website the same day.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "Hello,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nHere is our application for the Firefighters' Fund Open Race Half Marathon, Sunday 24 October 2027. 650 runners, half marathon, off at 09:30, around South Pier. I've attached ambulance_agreement.txt, crowd_plan.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt.\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you.\n\nThanks,\nTomas\n\nTomas Reyes, Halden Firefighters' Benevolent Fund\n555-0170\n",
